          en: 'To deepen the transition from junior to strategic, study systems thinking applied to software. Books like "Thinking in Systems" by Donella Meadows offer mental frameworks that transcend technology. Also study technical communication. the ability to articulate complex ideas clearly is one of the most undervalued skills in the market.\n\nSeek experiences outside your technical comfort zone. Participate in projects involving technologies you don\'t master. Lead code reviews. Document architectural decisions. Present to non-technical stakeholders. Each of these experiences adds a layer of maturity that cannot be obtained just by writing code.\n\nFinally, develop the habit of structured reflection. At the end of each sprint or project, ask yourself: what did I learn? What would I do differently? Where was I efficient and where did I waste effort? This practice of conscious self-evaluation is what separates professionals who grow from professionals who merely accumulate time.',
